A performance baseline represents the normal operating behaviour of an application or infrastructure. Establishing baselines helps administrators identify unusual activity and performance degradation more quickly.

Common baseline metrics include:

* CPU utilisation
* Memory usage
* Disk latency
* Network throughput
* Response time
* Error rate

For example, if a web application normally responds within 200 milliseconds but suddenly averages 800 milliseconds, administrators can investigate before users experience major disruption.

A real-life use case is operations teams using baseline data to distinguish between expected workload growth and abnormal behaviour.

Performance baselines improve proactive monitoring and troubleshooting.
